{"availability":"available","full":"ironsmile/euterpe","name":"euterpe","description":"Self-hosted music streaming server 🎶 with RESTful API and Web interface. Think of it as your very own Spotify! ☁️🎧","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":574,"forks":49,"created":"2014-01-01T12:51:54Z","updated":"2026-01-01T15:06:11Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://listen-to-euterpe.eu","topics":["http","listen","mp3","mp3player","music","self-hosted","streaming","streaming-audio"],"demo":"https://listen-to-euterpe.eu/demo","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:58.818Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:58.818Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:58.818Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:58.818Z","stars":574,"forks":49}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Euterpe is self-hosted streaming service for music.","A way to listen to your music library from everywhere. Once set up you won't need anything but a browser. Think of it as your own Spotify service over which you have full control. Euterpe will let you browse through and listen to your music over HTTP(s). Up until now I've had a really bad time listening to my music which is stored back home. I would create a mount over ftp, sshfs or something similar and point the local player to the mounted library. Every time it resulted in some unpleasantry. Just imagine searching in a network mounted directory!"],"features":["OSX Media Keys Control","Simple. It is just one binary, that's it! You don't need to faff about with interpreters or web servers","Fast. A typical response time on my more than a decade old mediocre computer is 26ms for a fairly large collection","Supports the most common audio formats such as mp3, oga, ogg, wav, flac, opus, web and m4a audio formats","Built-in fast and simple Web UI so that you can play your music on every device"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ironsmile/euterpe/blob/master/README.md